---
title: Writing shaders
description: Motion GPU WGSL entrypoints, coordinates, generated bindings, and color output.
---

This page documents the WGSL conventions added by Motion GPU. For WGSL language syntax and built-ins, use the WebGPU specification or a dedicated WGSL reference.

## Entrypoints

| Context | Required function |
| --- | --- |
| Material | `fn frag(uv: vec2f) -> vec4f` |
| `ShaderPass` | `fn shade(inputColor: vec4f, uv: vec2f) -> vec4f` |
| `PingPongShaderPass` | `fn frag(uv: vec2f) -> vec4f` |
| Compute pass | `@compute @workgroup_size(...) fn compute(...)` with a `global_invocation_id` parameter |

The material entrypoint is validated in the main `fragment` source before preprocessing, so do not place it inside an include. `PingPongShaderPass` validates its preprocessed source. `ShaderPass` and compute contracts are validated when their pass source is set.

## Coordinates

Material `uv` runs from `(0, 0)` at the bottom-left to `(1, 1)` at the top-right. `usePointer().state.current.uv` uses the same Y-up orientation. The final presentation pipeline preserves this public orientation even though internal render-target sampling follows framebuffer coordinates.

For aspect-correct calculations, use the physical render resolution:

```wgsl
let aspect = motiongpuFrame.resolution.x / motiongpuFrame.resolution.y;
```

## Generated bindings

Motion GPU injects the bindings it owns. Do not redeclare them.

### Frame uniforms

| Field | Type | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `motiongpuFrame.time` | `f32` | RAF timestamp in seconds |
| `motiongpuFrame.delta` | `f32` | Delta in seconds, clamped by `maxDelta` |
| `motiongpuFrame.resolution` | `vec2f` | Physical canvas resolution |

Material uniforms are fields of `motiongpuUniforms`. Each fragment-visible texture named `uImage` creates `uImage: texture_2d<f32>` and `uImageSampler: sampler` with a layout appropriate to the texture format.

Storage buffers are available by their declared names. Fragment shaders receive read-only bindings; compute access follows each definition.

### Feedback bindings

`PingPongShaderPass` exposes its previous state separately:

```wgsl
@group(1) @binding(0) var motiongpuPreviousSampler: sampler;
@group(1) @binding(1) var motiongpuPrevious: texture_2d<f32>;
```

The target material texture is excluded from that pass's regular texture bindings while it is being written. Sample prior state through `motiongpuPrevious`.

## Color and alpha

Author material and `ShaderPass` output in straight alpha. Motion GPU premultiplies only the final canvas presentation output.

Shader output is linear color. In the standard SDR path, `color.outputEncoding: 'srgb'` applies linear-to-sRGB encoding. A configured working format, tone mapper, or HDR mode moves final conversion into the private presentation pass after post-processing.

`canvasColorSpace` configures the canvas presentation space; it does not replace value encoding. The built-in Khronos PBR Neutral, Uncharted 2 / Hable Filmic, Stephen Hill ACES fit, and Gran Turismo tone mappers accept non-negative linear Rec.709 HDR input and produce SDR output, so they cannot be combined with explicit HDR canvas presentation.

Open the [Motion GPU Logo demo](/playground?demo=motion-gpu-logo&framework=svelte) for editable shader source. Resource-specific contracts are documented under [Uniforms](/docs/uniforms), [Textures](/docs/textures), and [Shader Includes & Defines](/docs/shader-includes-and-defines).
